@meta
id: 23-10
title: Jump between misspellings
chapter: 23
type: lesson
skills: spell
par: 28
minutes: 4
vscode: red squiggles from the Code Spell Checker extension, if installed
open: refunds.md
vimrc: set spell

@brief
Four words in this doc are misspelled. Spell checking is on for this
lesson, so they are underlined. Fix all four, in order, without typing
any of the corrections yourself: for each one, vim's first suggestion
is the right word.

@keys
| `]s` `[s` | next, previous misspelled word |
| `z=` | list the suggestions and pick one by number |
| `1z=` | take the first suggestion without looking |
| `:set spell` / `:set nospell` | switch it on and off yourself |

@hints
`]s` jumps straight to the first misspelled word. You do not need to
find it by eye.
--
`z=` on the word shows a numbered list; `1z=` takes entry one without
showing the list.
--
`]s1z=` four times.

@solution
    ]s1z= ]s1z= ]s1z= ]s1z= :wq<Enter>

Twenty-four keystrokes for four corrections.

`]s` and `[s` treat misspellings the way `n` and `N` treat search
matches, so you never scan for the red underline yourself. `z=` shows
a numbered menu of suggestions; the number you type picks one. A count
in front skips the menu, and `1z=` — take the first suggestion — is
right often enough to be a reflex for the everyday typos: transposed
letters, a doubled consonant, a missing vowel. Look at the menu when
the word is unusual.

Spell checking in a code file is syntax-aware: only comments and
strings are checked, so identifiers do not light up. In markdown the
whole text is checked, except for code blocks. `spelllang` defaults to
English; `set spelllang=en_gb` narrows it.

`set spell` is a good line for your vimrc, restricted to the file
types where prose lives: markdown, git commit messages, plain text.
Chapter 28 covers doing that per filetype.

@start refunds.md
# Refunds

A refund is proccessed by the payment provider, not by us. We record the
request, hand it to the provider, and store the reciept id on the order
when the provider calls back.

Orders are cancelled immediatly. The refund itself can take up to five
working days, and the customer is told this seperately in the email that
confirms the cancellation.

If the provider rejects the refund the order stays cancelled and the
reason is recorded for finance.

@expected refunds.md
# Refunds

A refund is processed by the payment provider, not by us. We record the
request, hand it to the provider, and store the receipt id on the order
when the provider calls back.

Orders are cancelled immediately. The refund itself can take up to five
working days, and the customer is told this separately in the email that
confirms the cancellation.

If the provider rejects the refund the order stays cancelled and the
reason is recorded for finance.
